{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["And the reason for <b>\"And it came to pass, when Moses had finished writing\"</b> is that at first he wrote the Torah and gave it to the priests, as is stated above (Deuteronomy 31:9), but he did not tell them where to place it. After that, he was commanded concerning this song, and he wrote it and taught it to the children of Israel on that very day, and behold, he added it to the Torah. And it came to pass, when Moses had finished writing everything in the book of the Torah, then he commanded the priests to take this book of the Torah and to place it at the side of the ark of the covenant of YHWH your Elohim, so that it would rest in the ark from the side, for from now on they would not touch it at all, neither to add nor to subtract. And this is the reason for \"And it came to pass, when Moses had finished writing,\" and so on, until \"to the very end.\" And therefore Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Deuteronomy 31:1) said that \"And this is the blessing\" is transposed, and its proper place is above, as it is said, \"And Moses went and spoke all these words to all Israel.\" And it is possible that after he wrote the song and taught it to the children of Israel, each man according to his tribe — for he had brought them before him into the house of study — he wrote it in the book of the Torah and commanded the priests to take the book of the Torah, to say that the song too should be placed in the ark together with the Torah, for it is part of the totality of the Torah, since it is there for a witness. And he told them that they should assemble to him again all the elders of the tribes and the officers, and the people would gather with them, for so it is stated at the end (Deuteronomy 32:44), \"And Moses came and spoke all the words of this song in the ears of the people.\" And behold, the priests did so, and they assembled to him all the people, and he called the heavens and the earth as witnesses against them, when he assembled them in the ears of the priests and all the people. And then HaShem, blessed be He, said to him (ibid. v. 49), \"Go up to this mountain of Avarim,\" and he was obligated to do so immediately. And he rose and blessed them — \"And this is the blessing\" — and he wrote it at the end of the book that he had given to the priests. And then the priests did what he had commanded them, and they placed the complete book at the side of the ark of the covenant. And behold, everything is according to the order stated in the Torah:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:57:45.869144605Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}